MixPi backport of upstream Mixxx commit bef0af317269dba735b06352f775d698c26f7406
"EngineBuffer: Reset sample counter after indicator update"
Author: Andrej Lajovic <andrej.lajovic@ad-vega.si>, 28 Mar 2026
Upstream: https://github.com/mixxxdj/mixxx/pull/16245 (merged into the 2.5
branch on 2 Jun 2026; not in 2.5.6). Fixes https://github.com/mixxxdj/mixxx/issues/9751
("Waveform Overview stops progressing").

Taken as it is: the upstream diff applies to the pinned tree (3ebac449, 2.5.6)
with every MixPi patch before it, with no change and no offset. It touches
src/engine/enginebuffer.cpp only.

Why: m_iSamplesSinceLastIndicatorUpdate is a signed int that was never reset
after the playposition update (the reset was lost in 5a4444d520, Jan 2019).
It grows by the buffer size on every callback while a track is loaded, so it
overflows after 2^31 samples (about 6 h 46 min at 44.1 kHz stereo) without a
seek. While it is negative, [ChannelN],playposition and CueControl's
indicators stop updating, and the DECKS overview strip freezes. With the
reset, both update at kPlaypositionUpdateRate (15 per second) and the counter
never exceeds about 5,880 samples plus one buffer.

diff --git a/src/engine/enginebuffer.cpp b/src/engine/enginebuffer.cpp
index 83bd03b..78cdc72 100644
--- a/src/engine/enginebuffer.cpp
+++ b/src/engine/enginebuffer.cpp
@@ -80,6 +80,7 @@ EngineBuffer::EngineBuffer(const QString& group,
           m_baserate_old(0),
           m_rate_old(0.),
           m_trackEndPositionOld(mixxx::audio::kInvalidFramePos),
+          m_iSamplesSinceLastIndicatorUpdate(0),
           m_slipPos(mixxx::audio::kStartFramePos),
           m_dSlipRate(1.0),
           m_bSlipEnabledProcessing(false),
@@ -1479,6 +1480,7 @@ void EngineBuffer::updateIndicators(double speed, int iBufferSize) {
                     kPlaypositionUpdateRate)) {
         m_playposSlider->set(fFractionalPlaypos);
         m_pCueControl->updateIndicators();
+        m_iSamplesSinceLastIndicatorUpdate = 0;
     }
 
